course: dictionary
lesson: 8345
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Rook is one word with three main meanings: a bird, a chess piece, and an old-fashioned word for cheating someone. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer wants. «In autumn farmers plough and sow winter wheat or barley, and gulls and rooks follow the plough to snatch worms and grubs.» Here rooks are birds, because they follow the plough to snatch worms.
explain: Look for clue words. If the text mentions a board, pawns or castling, the rook is a chess piece. If it mentions birds, a noisy group or a nest, it is the bird. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
explain: Rook as a verb is informal and old-fashioned, so you will meet it less often. To rook someone means to cheat them out of money. If a sentence is about someone losing money through a trick, rook may be the word to think of.
fact: A rook is a large black bird of the crow family, with a grey, bare patch of skin at the base of its beak.
fact: Rooks live together in noisy groups, and their nests at the tops of trees are called a rookery.
fact: In chess, a rook is shaped like a castle tower and moves straight along rows and columns. It is also called a castle.
fact: In the water jar test, «rooks and crows dropped stones into a tube» to raise a floating treat, like the crow in Aesop's fable.
fact: To rook someone is an informal, old-fashioned verb meaning to cheat them out of money.
exercise: «In autumn farmers plough and sow winter wheat or barley, and gulls and rooks follow the plough to snatch worms and grubs.» What is a rook in this sentence? | A kind of wheat | To cheat someone out of money | *A large black bird of the crow family | A chess piece shaped like a tower
exercise: «In experiments, rooks and crows dropped stones into a tube of water to raise a floating treat.» What are rooks in this sentence? | A kind of stone | *Birds from the crow family | Chess pieces | Floating treats
exercise: A player moves the rook straight along a row of the chessboard. What is a rook? | A bird with a bare grey patch by its beak | *A chess piece shaped like a castle tower | A large tree | To cheat someone out of money
test: Rooks live in noisy groups, and their nests are called a rookery. Where are the nests usually built? | *At the tops of trees | Under the water | Inside a chess box | On the ground in a cave
test: If someone tries to rook you, what are they trying to do? | *Cheat you out of money | Count the birds in a tree | Teach you to play chess | Give you a present
exam: Which clue in «rooks and crows dropped stones into a tube» tells you that rooks are birds? | *The word crows | The word stones | The word tube | The word water
